---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Crosswalk
permalink: /crosswalk/
---
{#- Generated: every term and vendor word comes from `_data/ecosystemMap.json5`, read from the term and vendor cards. #}
{%- import "macros/map.njk" as m %}
{%- set map = ecosystemMap %}

<section class="hero hero-compact" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 id="page-title">Crosswalk</h1>
    <p class="lede">Each term of the map, and what each vendor calls it.</p>
    <p>The terms are the industry's, in the map's reading order. A vendor's word is read from its own card, which links the term it matches: exactly, closely, as a narrower name such as a product's, or only as something related and easily mistaken for it. Each word links its card, which cites the vendor's own pages.</p>
    <aside class="notice" aria-label="Status">
      <p><strong>As of {{ map.source.committed | longDate }}.</strong> Drawn from the <a href="https://github.com/{{ map.source.repository }}/tree/{{ map.source.ref }}/{{ map.source.path }}/knowledge"><code>ki-agentic-ecosystems</code> knowledge map</a> at <code>{{ map.source.ref | truncate(9, true, "") }}</code>. A term or word still under review is marked as a draft.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="crosswalk-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="crosswalk-title" class="sr-only">The crosswalk</h2>
    <dl class="legend legend-matches" aria-label="Key">
      <div><dt>exact</dt><dd>means exactly the term</dd></div>
      <div><dt>close</dt><dd>means nearly the term</dd></div>
      <div><dt>narrower</dt><dd>a name for one kind of it, such as a product</dd></div>
      <div><dt>related</dt><dd>only related, and easily mistaken for it</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="matrix-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby="crosswalk-caption" tabindex="0">
      <table class="crosswalk">
        <caption id="crosswalk-caption">{{ map.crosswalk.length }} terms across {{ map.vendors.length }} vendors' cards.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Term</th>
            {%- for vendor in map.vendors %}
            <th scope="col">{{ vendor }}</th>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for term in map.crosswalk %}
          <tr id="term-{{ term.slug }}">
            <th scope="row" class="crosswalk-term">
              <a href="{{ term.url }}">{{ term.label }}</a>{% if term.status != "agreed" %} {{ m.statusBadge(term.status) }}{% endif %}
              <span class="crosswalk-summary">{{ term.summaryHtml | safe }}</span>
            </th>
            {%- for column in term.words %}
            <td>
              {%- if column.entries.length %}
              <ul class="words">
                {%- for entry in column.entries %}
                <li><a data-plain href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.word }}</a> <span class="match match-{{ entry.match }}">{{ entry.match }}</span>{% if entry.status != "agreed" %} {{ m.statusBadge(entry.status) }}{% endif %}</li>
                {%- endfor %}
              </ul>
              {%- else %}
              <span class="none" aria-label="No card">–</span>
              {%- endif %}
            </td>
            {%- endfor %}
          </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="section-intro">A dash means no vendor card for that vendor links the term yet, not that the vendor has no word for it.</p>
  </div>
</section>
